      "content": "Thanks, that's a good start. Regarding those distributed locking mechanisms and the latency issues mentioned—can you go deeper into the failure modes? \n\nI'm specifically interested in those hard-to-track, unpredictable edge cases that occur during a network partition. Sometimes it feels like the system experiences these sudden, tiny, disruptive errors that are incredibly difficult to replicate in staging but wreak havoc in production. How would you technically describe those types of intermittent, disruptive failures in a professional brief?",
